A||N||4||no_rice||3.4 in an '84||||1||
Z||000000||no_rice||06-26-2001||02:53 AM||||my friend has an '84 fiero w/ no engine and a tranny that needs rebuilt. a) should i buy it and b) i would put a 3.4L camaro engine in it put nitrous in it. does anyone know the horsepower or torque that would put out?||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfixit58||06-26-2001||07:44 AM||||no_rice,<P>First, WELCOME. Now on to your questions...<P>The 84 only came with the 4 cylinder so changing it to a 3.4 won't be as simple as retrofitting a later V-6 car. Although the block of the 3.4 is essentially the same you'll still have to use most of the exterior covers, brackets and pulleys from the 2.8. (see: <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#34" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#34</A>  )<P>Another solution, especially if it's an automatic is to drop in a 4.5 - 4.9 V-8 Cadillac motor. With an automatic is almost a straight drop in replacement for a 4 cylinder car. (see: <A HREF="http://sites.netscape.net/bubbajoexx/homepage" TARGET=_blank>http://sites.netscape.net/bubbajoexx/homepage</A>  )<P>Nitrous? Well, that's another topic better answered by some of of out other members.<P>Again, welcome,<BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||6
Z||000002||Seanh||07-02-2001||01:46 PM||||In case your still wondering, the engine lays down 195 HP and 200 ft/lbs the way I have it set up. I don't got no exhaust system for it, but those numbers are for the engine if you had headers w/equal length primaries. Now with NOS, depending on how much HP shot you went with. It could easialy take 150 HP NOS, its forged everything & 8.5:1 compression.<P>Could put the NorthStar in it too, if you feel like rebuilding a Dual overhead cam engine. I'd like to see Steve try doing something with that engine, it would be really funny. Perhaps we could get him to bore out the injectors with a drill?! (inside joke guys)||||reg||1
